  "method_caveats": [
    "Imbalanced ground truth bias: ground truth excludes (country, event_category) cells where the country never had ANY event of that category (pre or post cutoff). High-base-rate categories (e.g. bilateral_treaty ~0.72) suppress discrimination signal. Mean AUC is therefore a LOWER bound on per-cell predictive power.",
    "Reliability diagram is cross-category and reflects category-base-rate mixing, NOT per-category calibration. Bin-level event_rate values mix cells from categories with very different base rates. ECE here measures aggregate miscalibration, not per-category.",
    "Scoring formula uses |z_score| (magnitude), losing direction. An indicator that predicts events when HIGH (e.g. debt-to-GDP) is treated identically to one that predicts events when LOW (e.g. democracy index). Signed scoring is methodology v2.",
    "No baseline comparison: a uniform-weight or random-weight baseline AUC would tell us whether low AUC is caused by the weights being noise or by the scoring formula being the bottleneck. Tracked as follow-up ticket #598."
